WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.560
You've got a hundred receipts and you need
the numbers out of every one.

2
00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:04.700
Two ways to do this.

3
00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:05.980
Neither is good.

4
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:08.020
Set up a ChatGPT API account,

5
00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:10.500
add a card, pay by the token —

6
00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:11.760
forty-seven dollars.

7
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.120
Or upload them to ChatGPT yourself,

8
00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:15.140
one at a time.

9
00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:17.500
There goes your afternoon.

10
00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:19.820
But what if you could
automate the web app?

11
00:00:20.460 --> 00:00:21.540
That's Hermex.

12
00:00:21.540 --> 00:00:25.260
A Python library that drives
the ChatGPT and Gemini web apps.

13
00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.460
Not the API — the app itself.

14
00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:31.080
It types your prompt into the chat box
and hands the answer to your script.

15
00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:32.400
No API key.

16
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:33.480
No billing.

17
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:35.360
It runs on the account you already use.

18
00:00:36.420 --> 00:00:38.800
Ask it a question,
and get a straight answer.

19
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:39.960
That's one line of code.

20
00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:42.600
Send it a PDF and ask for the summary.

21
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:43.940
Also one line.

22
00:00:43.940 --> 00:00:47.240
Or point it at a hundred prompts
and write every image to disk.

23
00:00:47.240 --> 00:00:48.520
Still one line.

24
00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:50.300
It's free, open source,

25
00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.020
and one pip install away.

26
00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:54.460
No account to make, no key to copy.

27
00:00:54.460 --> 00:00:55.640
That's the whole setup.

28
00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:56.540
Head to the docs.

29
00:00:56.540 --> 00:00:57.960
You'll be running in minutes.

30
00:00:57.960 --> 00:00:59.071
Not an afternoon.
